    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Let $P(x)$ be the dividend. Then we can write \n\\[P(x) = (2x^2 - 7x + 18)(x^r + b) + Q(x)\\] \nfor some quotient $Q(x)$ and remainder $Q(x)$ such that $\\deg(Q) < \\deg(2x^2 - 7x + 18).$\nThe reminder can be $\\deg(1)$ or $\\deg(2).$\n\nOther great remarks!\n\nNo powers $x$ in the remainder, so the remainder is of degree $\\le 1$ and hence\n\\[P(x) = (2x^2 - 7x + 18)(x^r + b) + Q(x)\\]\nwhere $\\deg(Q(x))\\le1.$ So the degree of $P(x)$ is $\\deg(2x^2 -7x + 18)x^{r+1}+1,$ and hence the remainders has degree $\\le1,$ because the remainder same as $2x^2-7x+18$xdegno another variable. And also since the remainder doesn't contain $x$, it can't have another power such as $x^r+bx$.\nSo, the degree of $Q(x)$ at least minimum is $1$ and at most $0$\nBUT, the maximum of the degree of the reminder can never be $_04_\nThus, the only possible values are \n$0,1$.",
